Dear Dheeraj,

Your last working day has been approved as 01-11-2026 on the Employee Portal. To change your last working day, please have a discussion with your People Leader and raise a request<https://scsg.service-now.com/myhr?id=sc_cat_item&sys_id=65a312a3db69530027a49ceadb961980&sysparm_category=undefined>.

Please note that shortening your notice period may result in a reduction of your final settlement. Before you leave, we need you to complete some tasks and go through some details so that your exit from the Bank is as smooth as possible.

To help you manage your exit, we've given you access to your offboarding case<https://scbnow01.service-now.com/jny?id=jny_journey_details&sys_id=ce52d4d93b1f43506ef50044c3e45afc>. Here, you can access and manage the tasks that you need to complete as part of your exit formalities. You can also track all of the steps and the progress of your offboarding journey and communicate with your offboarding specialist via the "Activity" section.

Please be aware that Service Letters will be issued upon request only. You can request a Service Letter via the Alumni Portal.

Please look out for an email sent to your registered personal address after your last working day containing a link and detailed instructions on how to access the Alumni portal. Follow the steps and submit your Service Letter request.

We understand that you may have a lot of questions related to leaving, so we've prepared a helpful FAQ.<https://scsg.service-now.com/myhr?id=myhr_kb_article&sys_id=adc9fc0a877b251050adeac83cbb35ba> If you still have questions, just reach out to us via the activity section of your offboarding case and we will be happy to help.

Many Thanks,

Offboarding Team

This is a system generated email please do not respond to this. For specific questions please visit the offboarding case.



